fin-market-rules:RuleSelectionOutcomeShape a sh:NodeShape;
    sh:description "Rule Selection Outcome, is an immutable provenanced fact that records the result of evaluating one exact rule evaluation request against surviving applicability versions, used for making rule selection auditable. It is the abstract parent of the outcome hierarchy; exactly one concrete subtype is emitted per evaluation request, so that resolved selection, no-applicable-rule, and conflict are all first-class results rather than silent defaults.";
