    sh:description "Position Change, is a non-execution lifecycle event that changes a position's quantity or basis, used for tracing opening balance, transfer, corporate-action result, exercise or assignment, manual adjustment, clearing or custody statement, and calculated aggregation so that a position lot is not forced to be execution-derived. Full corporate-action workflow remains in an independent module; this association carries only the lot/position result and its source-event reference.";
