    sh:description "The settlement leg allocation is a generalization of trade settlement allocation that allocates any settlement leg (cash, security, fee, or tax) to an economic account, portfolio, beneficiary, or sub-settlement account, carrying the allocation basis, partial allocation, residual, and FX conversion. The existing TradeSettlementAllocation remains as the security-only execution-driven first profile specialization.";
