fin-post-trade:SettlementReconciliationComparatorShape a sh:NodeShape;
    sh:description "The settlement reconciliation comparator is a versioned comparator that locks settlement-reference normalization and canonical Money and Quantity rules, used for establishing the deterministic comparison baseline in settlement reconciliation. Under the Strict Technical Settlement Reconciliation Profile it additionally locks implementation, runtime, input-output contracts, and a zero numeric tolerance; those reproducibility fields (implementationDigest, runtimeDigest, inputContractDigest, outputContractDigest, referenceNormalizationDigest, canonicalizationDigest, numericTolerance) belong to the execution-and- reproducibility profile and are optional evidence in the generic core, so a real but not-yet-reproducibility- proven external report can still be expressed.";
