    sh:description "The trade settlement allocation is an exact allocation that allocates the execution quantity to the security leg, names both economic accounts, and independently selects direct equality or one PIT-eligible custody/omnibus bridge for each endpoint, used for placing an execution onto specific economic accounts.";
