fin-strategy:MetricDefinitionShape a sh:NodeShape;
    sh:description "Metric Definition, is a versioned specification that fixes the value representation and executable formula of one performance or attribution metric together with its metric kind, directionality, return convention, and annualization convention, used for locking the implementation, input and output contracts, runtime, and tool lock to ensure the metric is reproducible. The formula artifact is locatable and auditable via its reference and locator, not only its digest.";
    sh:name "Metric Definition";
